# What a Docker build may see. Dependencies are installed inside the image, so nothing from this machine's node_modules goes in, and
# no secret, no key, no local queue file and no evidence draft is ever sent to the Docker daemon.
# A leading slash anchors an entry to the root of the build context, so /src is the repository's own src and not packages/*/src.

/.git
/.github
/.vscode
/.claude

# Secrets and local state
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.key
**/*.pem
/.rehearsal
/.local-mainnet
/rehearsal-state.json
**/*.jsonl
**/*.lock
**/deployment.json
**/evidence-draft.json
**/KILL

# Built or installed output, rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
/artifacts
/cache

# Not needed to build or run the facilitator or the tool server
/contracts
/design
/docs
/scripts
/src
/test
/hardhat.config.ts
/eslint.config.mjs
/README.md
/DECISIONS.md
/AGENTS.md
/LICENSE

# The web app is deployed separately. Its manifest stays, because the lockfile names it as a workspace member.
/apps/web/*
!/apps/web/package.json
